WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.140
In 1975, the philosopher Peter Singer
argued that any being that can suffer has

2
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.430
interests.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.230
Favouring humans simply for being
human, he called speciesism.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.780
Today, health services compare treatments
by counting the years of good health

5
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.320
each one buys.

6
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:22.130
So if one person's suffering
would make thousands happier,

7
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.660
must a utilitarian say yes?

8
00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.120
In this mission, you'll meet
newer forms of utilitarianism,

9
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.790
built on preferences and interests.

10
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.750
Then you'll weigh whether
pleasure can be measured at all,

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.020
and what totals can justify.

12
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: find out
how utilitarians answer,

13
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.560
and why their critics push back.
